MulthiThreading Problem overcome with Synchronization
-  Synchronization

- Synchronization in Java is the process of controlling the access of multiple threads to shared resources. 
- It ensures that only one thread can access the critical section of code at a time, thus preventing data inconsistency and race conditions.

