-------------------------------------------Threre are two types of Synchronization------------------------------------------
1. Synchronized Methods
Idea: Only one thread is allowed to use the entire method at a time. Others have to wait.

Real-Life Example:

You and your friends are writing a group assignment in one shared Google Doc. To avoid confusion, you all agree that
only one person will edit at a time while others wait

Java Code:
 class Test {
	public synchronized void PrintTable(int n)
	{
		for (int i = 1; i <= 10; i++)
		{
			System.out.println(n * i);
		}
	}
}

class thread1 extends Thread
{
	Test t; // refernce banaye hai
	thread1(Test t)
	{
		this.t= t;	
	} 
	public void run()
	{
		t.PrintTable(5);
	}
}
class thread2 extends Thread
{
	Test t; // refernce banaye hai
